<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Mathematical Derivations</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Mathematical Setups</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The metric <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{St}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>St</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{St}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> measuring the variance of layer representations with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=1</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{St}^{2}\propto||h^{(1)}-h^{(0)}||^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mtext>St</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{St}^{2}\propto||h^{(1)}-h^{(0)}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the representation at layer <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>. Our goal is to compute the expected value <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\text{St}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mtext>St</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\text{St}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. For both Transformers and Mamba, the representation evolves as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(1)}=h^{(0)}+F(h^{(0)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(1)}=h^{(0)}+F(h^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">From our assumptions in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Backgrounds and Setups ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we have:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> are Gaussian matrices, <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h^{(0)}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h^{(0)}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Cov}(h^{(0)})=\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Cov}(h^{(0)})=\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}\sim N(0,\sigma^{2}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}\sim N(0,\sigma^{2}I)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is the update at layer <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> with deterministic parameters. We treat <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)</annotation></semantics></math> as random matrices with <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[F]=\mu_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[F]=\mu_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Cov}(F)=\Sigma_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Cov}(F)=\Sigma_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent for <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h^{(0)}_{j}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h^{(0)}_{j}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h_{i}h_{i}^{T}]=\sigma^{2}I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h_{i}h_{i}^{T}]=\sigma^{2}I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h^{(0)}_{j}(h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h^{(0)}_{j}(h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Objective:</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under some mild assumptions, we simplify and compare St<sup id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> from both architectures.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proofs</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmpropositioninner1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substitute into <a href="#A1.E16" title="In A.1 Mathematical Setups ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(1)}-h^{(0)}=(h^{(0)}+F(h^{(0)}))-h^{(0)}=F(h^{(0)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(1)}-h^{(0)}=(h^{(0)}+F(h^{(0)}))-h^{(0)}=F(h^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{St}^{2}\propto||h^{(1)}-h^{(0)}||^{2}=||F(h^{(0)})||^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mtext>St</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{St}^{2}\propto||h^{(1)}-h^{(0)}||^{2}=||F(h^{(0)})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}\to\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}\to\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the squared Frobenius norm is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||F(h^{(0)})||^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|F(h^{(0)})_{ij}|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||F(h^{(0)})||^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|F(h^{(0)})_{ij}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The expectation is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[||F(h^{(0)})||^{2}]=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i,j}|F(h^{(0)})_{ij}|^{2}\right]=\sum_{i,j}\mathbb{E}[|F(h^{(0)})_{ij}|^{2}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[||F(h^{(0)})||^{2}]=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i,j}|F(h^{(0)})_{ij}|^{2}\right]=\sum_{i,j}\mathbb{E}[|F(h^{(0)})_{ij}|^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> has deterministic parameters, the randomness in <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(h^{(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(h^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math> comes from <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The assumption states <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[F(h^{(0)})]=\mu_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[F(h^{(0)})]=\mu_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{F}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{F}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, so:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[F(h^{(0)})_{ij}]=(\mu_{F})_{ij}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[F(h^{(0)})_{ij}]=(\mu_{F})_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The variance of <math id="A1.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(h^{(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(h^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by a covariance matrix <math id="A1.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, but for a matrix-valued random variable, we interpret <math id="A1.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[|F(h^{(0)})_{ij}|^{2}]=\text{Var}(F(h^{(0)})_{ij})+|\mathbb{E}[F(h^{(0)})_{ij}]|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[|F(h^{(0)})_{ij}|^{2}]=\text{Var}(F(h^{(0)})_{ij})+|\mathbb{E}[F(h^{(0)})_{ij}]|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[|F(h^{(0)})_{ij}|^{2}]=\text{Var}(F(h^{(0)})_{ij})+|(\mu_{F})_{ij}|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[|F(h^{(0)})_{ij}|^{2}]=\text{Var}(F(h^{(0)})_{ij})+|(\mu_{F})_{ij}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Summing over all elements:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[||F(h^{(0)})||^{2}]=\sum_{i,j}\left(\text{Var}(F(h^{(0)})_{ij})+|(\mu_{F})_{ij}|^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[||F(h^{(0)})||^{2}]=\sum_{i,j}\left(\text{Var}(F(h^{(0)})_{ij})+|(\mu_{F})_{ij}|^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\text{St}^{2}]\propto\mathbb{E}\left[||F(h^{(0)})||^{2}\right]=\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F})+||(\mu_{F})||^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mtext>St</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\text{St}^{2}]\propto\mathbb{E}\left[||F(h^{(0)})||^{2}\right]=\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F})+||(\mu_{F})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p18.1" class="ltx_p">From <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof of Proposition . ‣ A.2 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, for Transformers:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\text{St}^{2}_{\text{Trans}}]\propto\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\text{Trans}})+||\mu_{F,\text{Trans}}||^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mtext>St</mtext><mtext>Trans</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Trans</mtext></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Trans</mtext></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\text{St}^{2}_{\text{Trans}}]\propto\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\text{Trans}})+||\mu_{F,\text{Trans}}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p20.1" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\text{Trans}}=\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})+\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)}),\quad\tilde{h}^{(0)}=h^{(0)}+\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>Trans</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>FFN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\text{Trans}}=\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})+\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)}),\quad\tilde{h}^{(0)}=h^{(0)}+\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{F,\text{Trans}}=\mathbb{E}[F_{\text{Trans}}]=\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})]+\mathbb{E}[\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Trans</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>Trans</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>FFN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{F,\text{Trans}}=\mathbb{E}[F_{\text{Trans}}]=\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})]+\mathbb{E}[\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)})]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{F,\text{Trans}}=\text{Cov}(\text{Attn}+\text{FFN})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Trans</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>FFN</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{F,\text{Trans}}=\text{Cov}(\text{Attn}+\text{FFN})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p21.1" class="ltx_p">For Mamba (a state-space model with selective mechanism):</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p22" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\text{St}^{2}_{\text{Mamba}}]\propto\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\text{Mamba}})+||\mu_{F,\text{Mamba}}||^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mtext>St</mtext><mtext>Mamba</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Mamba</mtext></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Mamba</mtext></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\text{St}^{2}_{\text{Mamba}}]\propto\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\text{Mamba}})+||\mu_{F,\text{Mamba}}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p23.1" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\text{Mamba}}=\text{S6}(h^{\prime})\circ z(h^{(0)}),\quad z=\text{SiLU}(\text{Linear}(h^{(0)})),\quad h^{\prime}=\text{SiLU}(\text{Conv1D}(\text{Linear}(h^{(0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>Mamba</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>S6</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Conv1D</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\text{Mamba}}=\text{S6}(h^{\prime})\circ z(h^{(0)}),\quad z=\text{SiLU}(\text{Linear}(h^{(0)})),\quad h^{\prime}=\text{SiLU}(\text{Conv1D}(\text{Linear}(h^{(0}))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{F,\text{Mamba}}=\mathbb{E}[\text{S6}\circ z]=\mathbb{E}[\text{S6}]\cdot\mathbb{E}[z]+\text{Cov}(S6,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Mamba</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>S6</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext>S6</mtext><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{F,\text{Mamba}}=\mathbb{E}[\text{S6}\circ z]=\mathbb{E}[\text{S6}]\cdot\mathbb{E}[z]+\text{Cov}(S6,z)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{F,\text{Mamba}}=\text{Cov}(\text{S6}\circ z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Mamba</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>S6</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{F,\text{Mamba}}=\text{Cov}(\text{S6}\circ z)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmpropositioninner2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the effect of negating the input: if we replace <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-x</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS2.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\text{new}}=(-x)W_{Q}=-xW_{Q}=-Q,\quad K_{\text{new}}=(-x)W_{K}=-xW_{K}=-K,\quad V_{\text{new}}=(-x)W_{V}=-xW_{V}=-V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\text{new}}=(-x)W_{Q}=-xW_{Q}=-Q,\quad K_{\text{new}}=(-x)W_{K}=-xW_{K}=-K,\quad V_{\text{new}}=(-x)W_{V}=-xW_{V}=-V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.SS2.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">The new attention scores become:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p27" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{(-Q)(-K)^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}=\frac{(-Q)(-K^{T})}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}=\frac{QK^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{(-Q)(-K)^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}=\frac{(-Q)(-K^{T})}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}=\frac{QK^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the softmax remains unchanged:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p29" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{softmax}\left(\frac{(-Q)(-K)^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{QK^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{softmax}\left(\frac{(-Q)(-K)^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{QK^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">The output is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p31" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Attn}(-x)=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{Q_{new}K_{new}^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)(V_{new})=-\text{softmax}\left(\frac{QK^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)V=-\text{Attn}(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Attn}(-x)=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{Q_{new}K_{new}^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)(V_{new})=-\text{softmax}\left(\frac{QK^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)V=-\text{Attn}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that the attention mechanism <math id="A1.SS2.p32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Attn(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Attn(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is odd.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmpropositioninner3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p33" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A1.SS2.p33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math> is odd and <math id="A1.SS2.p33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetrically distributed, we have <math id="A1.SS2.p33.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})]=\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}(h^{(1)})]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})]=\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}(h^{(1)})]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmtheoreminner1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p34" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p34.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p34.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="A1.SS2.p34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{F,\text{Trans}}=\mathbb{E}[F_{\text{Trans}}]=\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})]+\mathbb{E}[\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Trans</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>Trans</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>FFN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{F,\text{Trans}}=\mathbb{E}[F_{\text{Trans}}]=\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})]+\mathbb{E}[\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)})]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{h^{(0)}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{h^{(0)}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. From <a href="#Thmpropositioninner3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we have <math id="A1.SS2.p34.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p34.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\tilde{h}^{(0)})]=\mathbb{E}[{h}^{(0)}+\text{Attn}({h}^{(0)})]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mtext>Attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\tilde{h}^{(0)})]=\mathbb{E}[{h}^{(0)}+\text{Attn}({h}^{(0)})]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p35" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p35.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p35.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)})=W_{2}(\text{GELU}(W_{1}\tilde{h}^{(0)}+b_{1}))+b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>FFN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>GELU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)})=W_{2}(\text{GELU}(W_{1}\tilde{h}^{(0)}+b_{1}))+b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and assume that <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent, we approximate <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{GELU}(a)\approx a\cdot\sigma(1.702a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>GELU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1.702</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{GELU}(a)\approx a\cdot\sigma(1.702a)</annotation></semantics></math> following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks and Gimpel (2016)</a></cite>, and further approximate <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\cdot\sigma(1.702a)\approx\frac{1}{2}a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1.702</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\cdot\sigma(1.702a)\approx\frac{1}{2}a</annotation></semantics></math> via Taylor expansion via removing higher-order terms, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p36" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{F,Trans}=\mathbb{E}[\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>FFN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{F,Trans}=\mathbb{E}[\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[W_{2}\text{GELU}(W_{1}\tilde{h}^{(0)}+b_{1})+b_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>GELU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[W_{2}\text{GELU}(W_{1}\tilde{h}^{(0)}+b_{1})+b_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\mathbb{E}[W_{2}\frac{1}{2}(W_{1}\tilde{h}^{(0)}+b_{1})+b_{2}]=\frac{1}{2}W_{2}b_{1}+b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\mathbb{E}[W_{2}\frac{1}{2}(W_{1}\tilde{h}^{(0)}+b_{1})+b_{2}]=\frac{1}{2}W_{2}b_{1}+b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p36.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p36.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmtheoreminner2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p37" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p37.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p37.1.1" class="ltx_text">We need to compute <math id="A1.SS2.p37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\text{Trans}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Trans</mtext></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\text{Trans}})</annotation></semantics></math> for the Transformer-based model’s update function <math id="A1.SS2.p37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\text{Trans}}(h^{(0)})=\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})+\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>Trans</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>FFN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\text{Trans}}(h^{(0)})=\text{Attn}(h^{(0)})+\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math>. We have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p38" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(h^{(0)}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(h^{(0)}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t})+\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)}_{t})ß\approx\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t})+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}(W_{1}\tilde{h}^{(0)}_{t}+b_{1})+b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>FFN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ß</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t})+\text{FFN}(\tilde{h}^{(0)}_{t})ß\approx\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t})+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}(W_{1}\tilde{h}^{(0)}_{t}+b_{1})+b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t})+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}(h^{(0)_{t}}+\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t}))+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}b_{1}+b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t})+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}(h^{(0)_{t}}+\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t}))+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}b_{1}+b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(I+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}\right)\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t})+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}h^{(0)}_{t}+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}b_{1}+b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(I+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}\right)\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t})+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}h^{(0)}_{t}+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}b_{1}+b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\therefore F_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∴</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\therefore F_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T_{1}\text{Attn}_{t}+T_{2}h_{t}+\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T_{1}\text{Attn}_{t}+T_{2}h_{t}+\mu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p39" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p39.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p39.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}=I+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}=I+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}=\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}=\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p39.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\frac{1}{2}W_{2}b_{1}+b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\frac{1}{2}W_{2}b_{1}+b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also denote <math id="A1.SS2.p39.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t},\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t},\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> refers to <math id="A1.SS2.p39.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(h^{(0)}_{t}),\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t}),h^{(0)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>Attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(h^{(0)}_{t}),\text{Attn}(h^{(0)}_{t}),h^{(0)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively for ease of notation. We aim to compute <math id="A1.SS2.p39.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{F_{t}}=\mathbb{E}[F_{t}F_{t}^{T}]-\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{F_{t}}=\mathbb{E}[F_{t}F_{t}^{T}]-\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{t}F_{t}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{t}F_{t}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(T_{1}\text{Attn}_{t}+T_{2}h_{t}+\mu)(T_{1}\text{Attn}_{t}+T_{2}h_{t}+\mu)^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(T_{1}\text{Attn}_{t}+T_{2}h_{t}+\mu)(T_{1}\text{Attn}_{t}+T_{2}h_{t}+\mu)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\therefore\quad\mathbb{E}[F_{t}F_{t}^{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∴</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\therefore\quad\mathbb{E}[F_{t}F_{t}^{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T_{1}\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}_{t}\text{Attn}_{t}^{T}]T_{1}^{T}+T_{2}\mathbb{E}[hh^{T}]T_{2}^{T}+\mu\mu^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T_{1}\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}_{t}\text{Attn}_{t}^{T}]T_{1}^{T}+T_{2}\mathbb{E}[hh^{T}]T_{2}^{T}+\mu\mu^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T_{1}\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}T_{1}^{T}+T_{2}\Sigma_{h_{t}}T_{2}^{T}+\mu\mu^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T_{1}\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}T_{1}^{T}+T_{2}\Sigma_{h_{t}}T_{2}^{T}+\mu\mu^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p40" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p40.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p40.1.1" class="ltx_text">by using <math id="A1.SS2.p40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}_{t}]=\mathbb{E}[h_{t}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}_{t}]=\mathbb{E}[h_{t}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Attn}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Attn}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="A1.SS2.p40.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p41" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{F_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{F_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[F_{t}F_{t}^{T}]-\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[F_{t}F_{t}^{T}]-\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T_{1}\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}T_{1}^{T}+T_{2}\Sigma_{h_{t}}T_{2}^{T}+T_{1}\mathrm{Cov}(\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t})T_{2}^{T}+T_{2}\mathrm{Cov}(\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t})^{T}T_{1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T_{1}\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}T_{1}^{T}+T_{2}\Sigma_{h_{t}}T_{2}^{T}+T_{1}\mathrm{Cov}(\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t})T_{2}^{T}+T_{2}\mathrm{Cov}(\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t})^{T}T_{1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p42" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p42.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p42.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we need to compute the covariance of the attention output, <math id="A1.SS2.p42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given <math id="A1.SS2.p42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the attention output for a single token <math id="A1.SS2.p42.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p43" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Attn}_{t}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}a_{tj}h_{j}^{(0)}W_{V},\quad a_{tj}=\text{softmax}\Bigg(\frac{(h_{t}^{(0)}W_{Q})(h_{j}^{(0)}W_{K})^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\Bigg)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Attn}_{t}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}a_{tj}h_{j}^{(0)}W_{V},\quad a_{tj}=\text{softmax}\Bigg(\frac{(h_{t}^{(0)}W_{Q})(h_{j}^{(0)}W_{K})^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p44" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p44.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p44.1.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A1.SS2.p44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}_{t}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}_{t}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the covariance matrix is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p45" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}_{t}\text{Attn}_{t}^{T}]=\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\Bigg(\sum_{j=1}^{n}a_{tj}h_{j}^{(0)}W_{V}\Bigg)\Bigg(\sum_{k=1}^{n}a_{tk}h_{k}^{(0)}W_{V}\Bigg)^{T}\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}_{t}\text{Attn}_{t}^{T}]=\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\Bigg(\sum_{j=1}^{n}a_{tj}h_{j}^{(0)}W_{V}\Bigg)\Bigg(\sum_{k=1}^{n}a_{tk}h_{k}^{(0)}W_{V}\Bigg)^{T}\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\sum_{j,k=1}^{n}a_{tj}a_{tk}(h_{j}^{(0)}W_{V})(h_{k}^{(0)}W_{V})^{T}\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\sum_{j,k=1}^{n}a_{tj}a_{tk}(h_{j}^{(0)}W_{V})(h_{k}^{(0)}W_{V})^{T}\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p46" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p46.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p46.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS2.p46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{j}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{j}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent for <math id="A1.SS2.p46.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq k</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p46.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h_{j}^{(0)}]=\mathbb{E}[h_{k}^{(0)}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h_{j}^{(0)}]=\mathbb{E}[h_{k}^{(0)}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the cross-terms vanish unless <math id="A1.SS2.p46.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=k</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p47" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}^{2}]\mathbb{E}[(h_{j}^{(0)}W_{V})(h_{k}^{(0)}W_{V})^{T}]=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}^{2}](W_{V}\Sigma_{h^{(0)}}W_{V}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}^{2}]\mathbb{E}[(h_{j}^{(0)}W_{V})(h_{k}^{(0)}W_{V})^{T}]=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}^{2}](W_{V}\Sigma_{h^{(0)}}W_{V}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}^{2}](\sigma^{2}W_{V}W_{V}^{T})=\sigma^{2}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}^{2}]\right)W_{V}W_{V}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}^{2}](\sigma^{2}W_{V}W_{V}^{T})=\sigma^{2}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}^{2}]\right)W_{V}W_{V}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p48" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p48.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p48.1.1" class="ltx_text">The attention weights <math id="A1.SS2.p48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{tj}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{tj}</annotation></semantics></math> depend on the softmax output. For large <math id="A1.SS2.p48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, the dot product <math id="A1.SS2.p48.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h^{(0)}_{t}W_{Q})(h^{(0)}_{j}W_{K})^{T}/\sqrt{d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h^{(0)}_{t}W_{Q})(h^{(0)}_{j}W_{K})^{T}/\sqrt{d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> is approximately Gaussian. Assuming standard initialization <math id="A1.SS2.p48.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{Q},W_{K}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1/\sqrt{d}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{Q},W_{K}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1/\sqrt{d}))</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance of the dot product before scaling is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p49" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Var}((h_{t}^{(0)}W_{Q})(h_{j}^{(0)}W_{K})^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Var}((h_{t}^{(0)}W_{Q})(h_{j}^{(0)}W_{K})^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\sigma^{2}\cdot\frac{1}{d}\cdot\sigma^{2}\cdot d=\sigma^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\sigma^{2}\cdot\frac{1}{d}\cdot\sigma^{2}\cdot d=\sigma^{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\therefore\quad\text{Var}\Bigg(\frac{(h_{t}^{(0)}W_{Q})(h_{j}^{(0)}W_{K})^{T})}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∴</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\therefore\quad\text{Var}\Bigg(\frac{(h_{t}^{(0)}W_{Q})(h_{j}^{(0)}W_{K})^{T})}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{\sigma^{4}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{\sigma^{4}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p50" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p50.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p50.1.1" class="ltx_text">The softmax normalizes these scores, and for symmetrically distributed inputs, <math id="A1.SS2.p50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}]\approx 1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}]\approx 1/n</annotation></semantics></math>. The variance of the softmax output is small, and we approximate <math id="A1.SS2.p50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}^{2}]\approx 1/n^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}^{2}]\approx 1/n^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. And by assuming that <math id="A1.SS2.p50.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{V}W_{V}^{T}\approx I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{V}W_{V}^{T}\approx I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (standard initialization ensures <math id="A1.SS2.p50.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Tr}(W_{V}W_{V}^{T})\approx d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Tr}(W_{V}W_{V}^{T})\approx d</annotation></semantics></math>). The covariance <math id="A1.SS2.p50.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p51" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}\approx\sigma^{2}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\right)W_{V}W_{V}^{T}\approx\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}I_{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}\approx\sigma^{2}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\right)W_{V}W_{V}^{T}\approx\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p52" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p52.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p52.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we need to compute <math id="A1.SS2.p52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t})=\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}_{t}h_{t}]=\sum_{j=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}v_{j}h_{t}^{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t})=\mathbb{E}[\text{Attn}_{t}h_{t}]=\sum_{j=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}[a_{tj}v_{j}h_{t}^{T}]</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A1.SS2.p52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p52.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A1.SS2.p52.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and zero-mean so those terms are vanish. Thus, with <math id="A1.SS2.p52.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=t</annotation></semantics></math> and the same “mean-field” decoupling, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p53" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}(\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}(\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\mathbb{E}[a_{tt}]\mathbb{E}[v_{t}h_{t}^{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\mathbb{E}[a_{tt}]\mathbb{E}[v_{t}h_{t}^{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}W_{V}\mathbb{E}[h_{t}h_{t}^{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}W_{V}\mathbb{E}[h_{t}h_{t}^{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p54" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p54.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p54.1.1" class="ltx_text">Put everything together, we have the covariance trace for token <math id="A1.SS2.p54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p55" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Tr}(T_{1}\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}T_{1}^{T})+\text{Tr}(T_{2}\Sigma_{h_{t}}T_{2}^{T})+2\text{Tr}(T_{1}\mathrm{Cov}(\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t})T_{2}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Tr}(T_{1}\Sigma_{\text{Attn}_{t}}T_{1}^{T})+\text{Tr}(T_{2}\Sigma_{h_{t}}T_{2}^{T})+2\text{Tr}(T_{1}\mathrm{Cov}(\text{Attn}_{t},h_{t})T_{2}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}\text{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})+\sigma^{2}\text{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})+\frac{2\sigma^{2}}{n}\text{Tr}(T_{1}W_{V}T_{2}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}\text{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})+\sigma^{2}\text{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})+\frac{2\sigma^{2}}{n}\text{Tr}(T_{1}W_{V}T_{2}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p56" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p56.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p56.1.1" class="ltx_text">Sum over <math id="A1.SS2.p56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> across <math id="A1.SS2.p56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, we finally have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\text{Trans}})=\sigma^{2}\text{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})+n\sigma^{2}\text{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})+2\sigma^{2}\text{Tr}(T_{1}W_{V}T_{2}^{T})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Trans</mtext></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\text{Trans}})=\sigma^{2}\text{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})+n\sigma^{2}\text{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})+2\sigma^{2}\text{Tr}(T_{1}W_{V}T_{2}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p56.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p56.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmtheoreminner3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p57" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p57.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p57.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="A1.SS2.p57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{F,\text{Mamba}}=\mathbb{E}[\text{S6}\circ z]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Mamba</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>S6</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{F,\text{Mamba}}=\mathbb{E}[\text{S6}\circ z]</annotation></semantics></math>. The S6 layer can be represented as a data-controlled linear operator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Poli et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ali et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Specifically, for a sequence of inputs <math id="A1.SS2.p57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}=[h^{\prime}_{1},h^{\prime}_{2},\ldots,h^{\prime}_{n}]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}=[h^{\prime}_{1},h^{\prime}_{2},\ldots,h^{\prime}_{n}]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, the outputs <math id="A1.SS2.p57.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o=[o_{1},o_{2},\ldots,o_{n}]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=[o_{1},o_{2},\ldots,o_{n}]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> are computed through the following recursive equations. Assuming that <math id="A1.SS2.p57.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p58" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bar{B}_{1}h^{\prime}_{1},\quad o_{1}=C_{1}\bar{B}_{1}h^{\prime}_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bar{B}_{1}h^{\prime}_{1},\quad o_{1}=C_{1}\bar{B}_{1}h^{\prime}_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bar{A}_{2}\bar{B}_{1}h^{\prime}_{1}+\bar{B}_{2}h^{\prime}_{2},\quad o_{2}=C_{2}\bar{A}_{2}\bar{B}_{1}h^{\prime}_{1}+C_{2}\bar{B}_{2}h^{\prime}_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bar{A}_{2}\bar{B}_{1}h^{\prime}_{1}+\bar{B}_{2}h^{\prime}_{2},\quad o_{2}=C_{2}\bar{A}_{2}\bar{B}_{1}h^{\prime}_{1}+C_{2}\bar{B}_{2}h^{\prime}_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p59" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p59.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p59.1.1" class="ltx_text">These equations define <math id="A1.SS2.p59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(1)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(1)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> recursively using matrices <math id="A1.SS2.p59.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p59.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{B}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{B}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p59.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, applied to input vectors <math id="A1.SS2.p59.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The general form, given in Equation (10), is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p60" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{t}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}h^{\prime}_{j},\quad o_{t}=C_{t}\sum_{j=1}^{t}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}h^{\prime}_{j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{t}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}h^{\prime}_{j},\quad o_{t}=C_{t}\sum_{j=1}^{t}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}h^{\prime}_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p61" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p61.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p61.1.1" class="ltx_text">In matrix form, this can be expressed as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p62" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o=\hat{\alpha}h^{\prime}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=\hat{\alpha}h^{\prime},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p63" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p63.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p63.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is the matrix:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p64" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\alpha}=\begin{bmatrix}C_{1}\bar{B}_{1}&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;0\\
C_{2}\bar{A}_{2}\bar{B}_{1}&amp;C_{2}\bar{B}_{2}&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
C_{n}\bar{A}_{n}\bar{A}_{n-1}\cdots\bar{A}_{2}\bar{B}_{1}&amp;C_{n}\bar{A}_{n}\bar{A}_{n-1}\cdots\bar{A}_{3}\bar{B}_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;C_{n}\bar{B}_{n}\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\alpha}=\begin{bmatrix}C_{1}\bar{B}_{1}&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;0\\
C_{2}\bar{A}_{2}\bar{B}_{1}&amp;C_{2}\bar{B}_{2}&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
C_{n}\bar{A}_{n}\bar{A}_{n-1}\cdots\bar{A}_{2}\bar{B}_{1}&amp;C_{n}\bar{A}_{n}\bar{A}_{n-1}\cdots\bar{A}_{3}\bar{B}_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;C_{n}\bar{B}_{n}\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p65" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p65.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p65.1.1" class="ltx_text">The element at row <math id="A1.SS2.p65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and column <math id="A1.SS2.p65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS2.p65.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, as specified in Equation (12), is computed as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p66" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\alpha}_{i,j}=\begin{cases}C_{i}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{i}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}&amp;\text{if }i\geq j,\\
0&amp;\text{if }i&lt;j.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\alpha}_{i,j}=\begin{cases}C_{i}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{i}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}&amp;\text{if }i\geq j,\\
0&amp;\text{if }i&lt;j.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p67" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p67.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p67.1.1" class="ltx_text">This matrix <math id="A1.SS2.p67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\alpha}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\alpha}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of the input and the parameters <math id="A1.SS2.p67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{A},\bar{B},\bar{C},\bar{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{A},\bar{B},\bar{C},\bar{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, encapsulating the data-controlled linear transformations applied by the S6 layer at layer <math id="A1.SS2.p67.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p68" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p68.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p68.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we have <math id="A1.SS2.p68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\text{SiLU}(\text{Linear}(h^{(0)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\text{SiLU}(\text{Linear}(h^{(0)}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that <math id="A1.SS2.p68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Linear}(h^{(0)})=W_{z}h^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Linear}(h^{(0)})=W_{z}h^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.p68.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times ed}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times ed}</annotation></semantics></math> is a weight matrix and <math id="A1.SS2.p68.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> is the expansion factor (typically 2). Denote <math id="A1.SS2.p68.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\text{Linear}(h^{(0)})=W_{z}h^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\text{Linear}(h^{(0)})=W_{z}h^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>, by approximating SiLU function as <math id="A1.SS2.p68.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SiLU}(x)\approx\frac{x}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SiLU}(x)\approx\frac{x}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> via Taylor expansion, we have <math id="A1.SS2.p68.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}\approx\frac{u_{i}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}\approx\frac{u_{i}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, we have <math id="A1.SS2.p68.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[o_{i}z_{i}]\approx\mathbb{E}\left[o_{i}\frac{u_{i}}{2}\right]=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}[o_{i}u_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[o_{i}z_{i}]\approx\mathbb{E}\left[o_{i}\frac{u_{i}}{2}\right]=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}[o_{i}u_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Computing <math id="A1.SS2.p68.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[o\circ z]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[o\circ z]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p69" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[o\circ z]=\mathbb{E}\left[\begin{bmatrix}o_{1}z_{1}\\
\vdots\\
o_{n}z_{n}\end{bmatrix}\right]=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\begin{bmatrix}o_{1}u_{1}\\
\vdots\\
o_{n}u_{n}\end{bmatrix}\right]=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{diag}(\mathbb{E}[ou^{T}])" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[o\circ z]=\mathbb{E}\left[\begin{bmatrix}o_{1}z_{1}\\
\vdots\\
o_{n}z_{n}\end{bmatrix}\right]=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\begin{bmatrix}o_{1}u_{1}\\
\vdots\\
o_{n}u_{n}\end{bmatrix}\right]=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{diag}(\mathbb{E}[ou^{T}])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p70" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p70.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p70.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <a href="#A1.E48" title="In Proof of . ‣ A.2 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p71" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[o_{t}u_{t}^{T}]=\mathbb{E}\left[C_{t}\sum_{j=1}^{t}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}h^{\prime}_{j}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[o_{t}u_{t}^{T}]=\mathbb{E}\left[C_{t}\sum_{j=1}^{t}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}h^{\prime}_{j}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p72" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p72.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p72.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, for <math id="A1.SS2.p72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}=\text{SiLU}(\text{Conv1D}(\text{Linear}(h^{(0)})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Conv1D</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}=\text{SiLU}(\text{Conv1D}(\text{Linear}(h^{(0)})))</annotation></semantics></math>, assume that the linear transformation parameter is <math id="A1.SS2.p72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times ed}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times ed}</annotation></semantics></math> and the causal convolution with kernel size <math id="A1.SS2.p72.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (typically 4) is <math id="A1.SS2.p72.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, for the time <math id="A1.SS2.p72.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,2,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,2,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p73" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h^{\prime}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h^{\prime}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{SiLU}(\text{Conv1D}(\text{Linear}(h^{(0)}_{t})))=\text{SiLU}(W_{c}(W_{h}h^{(0)}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Conv1D</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{SiLU}(\text{Conv1D}(\text{Linear}(h^{(0)}_{t})))=\text{SiLU}(W_{c}(W_{h}h^{(0)}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{SiLU}\Bigg(\sum_{j=0}^{K-1}W_{c_{j}}(W_{h}h^{(0)}_{t-j})\Bigg)\approx\frac{1}{2}W_{c_{j}}W_{h}\sum_{j=0}^{K-1}h^{(0)}_{t-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{SiLU}\Bigg(\sum_{j=0}^{K-1}W_{c_{j}}(W_{h}h^{(0)}_{t-j})\Bigg)\approx\frac{1}{2}W_{c_{j}}W_{h}\sum_{j=0}^{K-1}h^{(0)}_{t-j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p74" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p74.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p74.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A1.SS2.p74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{h^{\prime}_{j}}=W_{c_{j}}W_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{h^{\prime}_{j}}=W_{c_{j}}W_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.p74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{h^{\prime}_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{h^{\prime}_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the combined transformation matrix. Thus:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p75" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[o_{t}u_{t}^{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[o_{t}u_{t}^{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[C_{t}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\left(\prod_{k=i+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{i}\left(\frac{1}{2}W_{h^{\prime}_{j}}\sum_{j=0}^{K-1}h^{(0)}_{i-j}\right)(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[C_{t}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\left(\prod_{k=i+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{i}\left(\frac{1}{2}W_{h^{\prime}_{j}}\sum_{j=0}^{K-1}h^{(0)}_{i-j}\right)(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}C_{t}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\sum_{j=0}^{K-1}\left(\prod_{k=i+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{i}W_{h^{\prime}_{j}}\mathbb{E}\left[h^{(0)}_{i-j}(h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]W_{z}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}C_{t}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\sum_{j=0}^{K-1}\left(\prod_{k=i+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{i}W_{h^{\prime}_{j}}\mathbb{E}\left[h^{(0)}_{i-j}(h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]W_{z}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p76" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p76.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p76.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under assumptions, in the sum over <math id="A1.SS2.p76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS2.p76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the expectation <math id="A1.SS2.p76.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h^{(0)}_{i-j}(h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h^{(0)}_{i-j}(h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}]</annotation></semantics></math> is either 0 when <math id="A1.SS2.p76.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-j\neq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-j\neq t</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="A1.SS2.p76.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.SS2.p76.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-j=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-j=t</annotation></semantics></math>, which means <math id="A1.SS2.p76.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=t,j=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=t,j=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p77" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[o_{t}u_{t}^{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[o_{t}u_{t}^{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}C_{t}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\sum_{j=0}^{K-1}\left(\prod_{k=i+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{i}W_{h^{\prime}_{j}}\mathbb{E}\left[h^{(0)}_{i-j}(h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]W_{z}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}C_{t}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\sum_{j=0}^{K-1}\left(\prod_{k=i+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{i}W_{h^{\prime}_{j}}\mathbb{E}\left[h^{(0)}_{i-j}(h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]W_{z}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}C_{t}\left(\prod_{k=i+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}_{0}}\mathbb{E}\left[h^{(0)}_{t}(h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]W_{z}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}C_{t}\left(\prod_{k=i+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}_{0}}\mathbb{E}\left[h^{(0)}_{t}(h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]W_{z}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}C_{t}\left(\prod_{k=i+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}_{0}}\sigma^{2}W_{z}^{T}=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}C_{t}\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}_{0}}W_{z}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}C_{t}\left(\prod_{k=i+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}_{0}}\sigma^{2}W_{z}^{T}=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}C_{t}\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}_{0}}W_{z}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p78" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p78.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p78.1.1" class="ltx_text">and <math id="A1.SS2.p78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{F,\text{Mamba}}=\mathbb{E}[\text{S6}\circ z]=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{diag}(\mathbb{E}[ou^{T}])=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{4n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathrm{diag}(C_{t}\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}_{0}}W_{z}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Mamba</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>S6</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{F,\text{Mamba}}=\mathbb{E}[\text{S6}\circ z]=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{diag}(\mathbb{E}[ou^{T}])=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{4n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathrm{diag}(C_{t}\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}_{0}}W_{z}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmtheoreminner4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p79" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p79.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p79.1.1" class="ltx_text">We need to compute <math id="A1.SS2.p79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\text{Mamba}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Mamba</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\text{Mamba}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for the Mamba model’s update function <math id="A1.SS2.p79.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\text{Mamba}}(h^{(0)})=o\circ z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>Mamba</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\text{Mamba}}(h^{(0)})=o\circ z</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.p79.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> is the output of the S6 layer and <math id="A1.SS2.p79.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> is the gating term, both dependent on the input <math id="A1.SS2.p79.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p80" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p80.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p80.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under the first-order nonlinearity approximation (S4), the Mamba update at time <math id="A1.SS2.p80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p81" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(h^{(0)}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(h^{(0)}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}(o_{t}\circ z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}(o_{t}\circ z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{diag}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})C_{t}\sum_{j=1}^{t}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}W_{h^{\prime}}h^{(0)}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{diag}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})C_{t}\sum_{j=1}^{t}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}W_{h^{\prime}}h^{(0)}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{diag}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})\sum_{j=1}^{t}M_{t,j}h^{(0)}_{j},\quad\text{where}\quad M_{t,j}=C_{t}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}W_{h^{\prime}}\in\mathbb{R}^{ed\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{diag}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})\sum_{j=1}^{t}M_{t,j}h^{(0)}_{j},\quad\text{where}\quad M_{t,j}=C_{t}\left(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k}\right)\bar{B}_{j}W_{h^{\prime}}\in\mathbb{R}^{ed\times d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E64.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{diag}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})M_{t,j}h^{(0)}_{j}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>diag</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{diag}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})M_{t,j}h^{(0)}_{j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p82" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p82.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p82.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> refers to <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(h^{(0)}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(h^{(0)}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> for ease of notation. For <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&lt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&lt;t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent, so expectation is zero. For <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=t</annotation></semantics></math>, both terms involves <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Writing row <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t,t}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{T}_{t,t,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{T}_{t,t,r}</annotation></semantics></math> and row <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS2.p82.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{T}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{T}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p83" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[F_{t,r}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[F_{t,r}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}[(m^{T}_{t,t,r}h^{(0)}_{t})(w^{T}_{r}h^{(0)}_{t})]=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}m^{T}_{t,t,r}w_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}[(m^{T}_{t,t,r}h^{(0)}_{t})(w^{T}_{r}h^{(0)}_{t})]=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}m^{T}_{t,t,r}w_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\therefore\quad\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∴</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\therefore\quad\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}\mathrm{diag}(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}\mathrm{diag}(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p84" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p84.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p84.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the second moment, use the identity <math id="A1.SS2.p84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{diag}(a)X\mathrm{diag}(b)=(ab^{T})\circ X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{diag}(a)X\mathrm{diag}(b)=(ab^{T})\circ X</annotation></semantics></math>, we can compute:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p85" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{t}F^{T}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{t}F^{T}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\mathrm{diag}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})\left(\sum_{j=1}^{t}M_{t,j}h^{(0)}_{j}\right)\left(\sum_{m=1}^{t}M_{t,m}h^{(0)}_{m}\right)^{T}\mathrm{diag}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\mathrm{diag}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})\left(\sum_{j=1}^{t}M_{t,j}h^{(0)}_{j}\right)\left(\sum_{m=1}^{t}M_{t,m}h^{(0)}_{m}\right)^{T}\mathrm{diag}(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\left[(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]\circ\left[\left(\sum_{j=1}^{t}M_{t,j}h^{(0)}_{j}\right)\left(\sum_{m=1}^{t}M_{t,m}h^{(0)}_{m}\right)^{T}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\left[(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})(W_{z}h^{(0)}_{t})^{T}\right]\circ\left[\left(\sum_{j=1}^{t}M_{t,j}h^{(0)}_{j}\right)\left(\sum_{m=1}^{t}M_{t,m}h^{(0)}_{m}\right)^{T}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p86" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p86.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p86.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now take expectation: (1) for <math id="A1.SS2.p86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq m</annotation></semantics></math>, cross terms vanish by independence and zero mean; (2) for <math id="A1.SS2.p86.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=m\neq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=m\neq t</annotation></semantics></math>, contributions are <math id="A1.SS2.p86.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{4}(W_{z}W^{T}_{z})\circ(\sum_{j=1}^{t-1}M_{t,j}M^{T}_{t,j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{4}(W_{z}W^{T}_{z})\circ(\sum_{j=1}^{t-1}M_{t,j}M^{T}_{t,j})</annotation></semantics></math>; (3) for <math id="A1.SS2.p86.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=m=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=m=t</annotation></semantics></math>, Isserlis’s theorem gives an extra correction term. For <math id="A1.SS2.p86.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I)</annotation></semantics></math> and vectors <math id="A1.SS2.p86.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c,d</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p87" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[(a^{T}x)(b^{T}x)(c^{T}x)(d^{T}x)\right]=\sigma^{4}\left[(a\cdot b)(c\cdot d)+(a\cdot c)(b\cdot d)+(a\cdot d)(b\cdot c)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[(a^{T}x)(b^{T}x)(c^{T}x)(d^{T}x)\right]=\sigma^{4}\left[(a\cdot b)(c\cdot d)+(a\cdot c)(b\cdot d)+(a\cdot d)(b\cdot c)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p88" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p88.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p88.1.1" class="ltx_text">With <math id="A1.SS2.p88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=m_{t,t,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=m_{t,t,r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=w_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=w_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p88.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=m_{t,t,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=m_{t,t,s}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p88.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=w_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=w_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A1.SS2.p88.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r,s)</annotation></semantics></math>-entry of <math id="A1.SS2.p88.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[(W_{z}h_{t})(W_{z}h_{t})^{T}\circ(M_{t,t}h_{t}h_{t}^{T}M_{t,t}^{T})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[(W_{z}h_{t})(W_{z}h_{t})^{T}\circ(M_{t,t}h_{t}h_{t}^{T}M_{t,t}^{T})\big]</annotation></semantics></math> equals</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p89" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{4}\left[(m_{t,t,r}\cdot w_{r})(m_{t,t,s}\cdot w_{s})+(m_{t,t,r}\cdot m_{t,t,s})(w_{r}\cdot w_{s})+(m_{t,t,r}\cdot w_{s})(w_{r}\cdot m_{t,t,s})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{4}\left[(m_{t,t,r}\cdot w_{r})(m_{t,t,s}\cdot w_{s})+(m_{t,t,r}\cdot m_{t,t,s})(w_{r}\cdot w_{s})+(m_{t,t,r}\cdot w_{s})(w_{r}\cdot m_{t,t,s})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p90" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p90.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p90.1.1" class="ltx_text">In matrix form, the three terms correspond to</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p91" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{4}\left[vv^{T}+(M_{t,t}M_{t,t}^{T})\circ(W_{z}W_{z}^{T})+(M_{t,t}W_{z}^{T})\circ(W_{z}M_{t,t}^{T})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{4}\left[vv^{T}+(M_{t,t}M_{t,t}^{T})\circ(W_{z}W_{z}^{T})+(M_{t,t}W_{z}^{T})\circ(W_{z}M_{t,t}^{T})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p92" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p92.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p92.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\mathrm{diag}(M_{t,t}W_{z}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\mathrm{diag}(M_{t,t}W_{z}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math>. Putting everything together, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p93" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[F_{t}F^{T}_{t}]=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\left[vv^{T}+S_{t}\circ(W_{z}W^{T}_{z})+(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})\circ(W_{z}M^{T}_{t,t,})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[F_{t}F^{T}_{t}]=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\left[vv^{T}+S_{t}\circ(W_{z}W^{T}_{z})+(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})\circ(W_{z}M^{T}_{t,t,})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p94" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p94.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p94.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=\left(\sum_{j=1}^{t-1}M_{t,j}M^{T}_{t,j}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=\left(\sum_{j=1}^{t-1}M_{t,j}M^{T}_{t,j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p94.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\mathrm{diag}(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\mathrm{diag}(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p95" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p95.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p95.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p96" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]^{T}=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\mathrm{diag}(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})[\mathrm{diag}(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})]^{T}=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}vv^{T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]^{T}=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\mathrm{diag}(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})[\mathrm{diag}(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})]^{T}=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}vv^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p97" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p97.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p97.1.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting this, we have the covariance as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p98" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{F_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{F_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E71.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cov}(F_{t})=\mathbb{E}[F_{t}F_{t}^{T}]-\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cov}(F_{t})=\mathbb{E}[F_{t}F_{t}^{T}]-\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]\mathbb{E}[F_{t}]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\left[(W_{z}W^{T}_{z})\circ S_{t}+(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})\circ(W_{z}M^{T}_{t,t})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\left[(W_{z}W^{T}_{z})\circ S_{t}+(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})\circ(W_{z}M^{T}_{t,t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p99" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p99.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p99.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take the trace and sum over <math id="A1.SS2.p99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,Mamba})=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\{\text{Tr}[(W_{z}W^{T}_{z})\circ S_{t}]+\text{Tr}[(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})\circ(W_{z}M^{T}_{t,t})]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,Mamba})=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\{\text{Tr}[(W_{z}W^{T}_{z})\circ S_{t}]+\text{Tr}[(M_{t,t}W^{T}_{z})\circ(W_{z}M^{T}_{t,t})]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p99.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p99.2.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A1.SS2.p99.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=\left(\sum_{j=1}^{t-1}M_{t,j}M^{T}_{t,j}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=\left(\sum_{j=1}^{t-1}M_{t,j}M^{T}_{t,j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p100" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p100.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p100.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.9" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmtheoreminner5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p101" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p101.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p101.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given that <math id="A1.SS2.p101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\text{St}^{2}]=||\mu_{F}||^{2}+\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mtext>St</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\text{St}^{2}]=||\mu_{F}||^{2}+\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F})</annotation></semantics></math>, we first rearrange all the equations we obtained.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(1) Transformer’s mean.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#Thmtheoreminner1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{F,\mathrm{Trans}}\approx\tfrac{1}{2}W_{2}b_{1}+b_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Trans</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{F,\mathrm{Trans}}\approx\tfrac{1}{2}W_{2}b_{1}+b_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using independence and centering,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\mu_{F,\mathrm{Trans}}\|_{2}^{2}\right]=\tfrac{1}{4}\,\mathbb{E}[\|W_{2}b_{1}\|_{2}^{2}]+\mathbb{E}[\|b_{2}\|_{2}^{2}]=\alpha_{T}&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Trans</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\mu_{F,\mathrm{Trans}}\|_{2}^{2}\right]=\tfrac{1}{4}\,\mathbb{E}[\|W_{2}b_{1}\|_{2}^{2}]+\mathbb{E}[\|b_{2}\|_{2}^{2}]=\alpha_{T}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(2) Transformer’s covariance.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#Thmtheoreminner2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Trans}})=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})+n\sigma^{2}\mathrm{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})+2\sigma^{2}\mathrm{Tr}(T_{1}W_{V}T_{2}^{T})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Trans</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Trans}})=\sigma^{2}\mathrm{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})+n\sigma^{2}\mathrm{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})+2\sigma^{2}\mathrm{Tr}(T_{1}W_{V}T_{2}^{T}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The cross term is linear in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and independent of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1},W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1},W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[W_{V}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[W_{V}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Trans}})]=\sigma^{2}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})]+n\sigma^{2}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Trans</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Trans}})]=\sigma^{2}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})]+n\sigma^{2}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Now computing:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{Tr}\left[\left(I+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}\right)\left(I+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}\right)^{T}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{Tr}\left[\left(I+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}\right)\left(I+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}\right)^{T}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{Tr}\left[I+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}+\frac{1}{2}(W_{2}W_{1})^{T}+\frac{1}{4}(W_{2}W_{1})(W_{2}W_{1})^{T}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{Tr}\left[I+\frac{1}{2}W_{2}W_{1}+\frac{1}{2}(W_{2}W_{1})^{T}+\frac{1}{4}(W_{2}W_{1})(W_{2}W_{1})^{T}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d+\mathrm{Tr}(W_{2}W_{1})+\frac{1}{4}\|W_{2}W_{1}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d+\mathrm{Tr}(W_{2}W_{1})+\frac{1}{4}\|W_{2}W_{1}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\|W_{2}W_{1}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\|W_{2}W_{1}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Putting together, we get:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Trans}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Trans</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Trans}})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})]+n\sigma^{2}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(T_{1}T_{1}^{T})]+n\sigma^{2}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(T_{2}T_{2}^{T})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[d+\mathrm{Tr}(W_{2}W_{1})+\frac{(n+1)}{4}\|W_{2}W_{1}\|_{F}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[d+\mathrm{Tr}(W_{2}W_{1})+\frac{(n+1)}{4}\|W_{2}W_{1}\|_{F}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma^{2}n}{4}\mathbb{E}[\|W_{2}W_{1}\|_{F}^{2}]+\sigma^{2}\left[\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(W_{2}W_{1})]+\frac{1}{4}\mathbb{E}[\|W_{2}W_{1}\|_{F}^{2}]+d\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma^{2}n}{4}\mathbb{E}[\|W_{2}W_{1}\|_{F}^{2}]+\sigma^{2}\left[\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(W_{2}W_{1})]+\frac{1}{4}\mathbb{E}[\|W_{2}W_{1}\|_{F}^{2}]+d\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma^{2}n}{4}\beta_{T}+\sigma^{2}\gamma_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sigma^{2}n}{4}\beta_{T}+\sigma^{2}\gamma_{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{T}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{T}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{T}\geq d&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{T}\geq d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are constants, given that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1},W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1},W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent and centered.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(3) Mamba’s mean.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#Thmtheoreminner3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}}\approx\frac{\sigma^{2}}{4n}\sum_{t}\mathrm{diag}(C_{t}\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}}^{0}W_{z}^{T})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Mamba</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}}\approx\frac{\sigma^{2}}{4n}\sum_{t}\mathrm{diag}(C_{t}\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}}^{0}W_{z}^{T}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using Jensen and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{diag}(X)\|_{2}\leq\|X\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{diag}(X)\|_{2}\leq\|X\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mu_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}}\|_{2}^{2}\leq\frac{\sigma^{4}}{16n^{2}}\sum_{t}\|C_{t}\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}}^{0}W_{z}^{T}\|_{F}^{2}\leq\frac{\sigma^{4}}{16n^{2}}\alpha_{M}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Mamba</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mu_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}}\|_{2}^{2}\leq\frac{\sigma^{4}}{16n^{2}}\sum_{t}\|C_{t}\bar{B}_{t}W_{h^{\prime}}^{0}W_{z}^{T}\|_{F}^{2}\leq\frac{\sigma^{4}}{16n^{2}}\alpha_{M}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{M}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{M}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(4) Mamba’s covariance.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#Thmtheoreminner4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 4.2 Theoretical Results ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t,j}=C_{t}(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k})\bar{B}_{j}W_{h^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t,j}=C_{t}(\prod_{k=j+1}^{t}\bar{A}_{k})\bar{B}_{j}W_{h^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=\sum_{j&lt;t}M_{t,j}M_{t,j}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=\sum_{j&lt;t}M_{t,j}M_{t,j}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}})=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\left\{\mathrm{Tr}[(W_{z}W_{z}^{T})\circ S_{t}]+\mathrm{Tr}[(M_{t,t}W_{z}^{T})\circ(W_{z}M_{t,t}^{T})]\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Mamba</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}})=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\left\{\mathrm{Tr}[(W_{z}W_{z}^{T})\circ S_{t}]+\mathrm{Tr}[(M_{t,t}W_{z}^{T})\circ(W_{z}M_{t,t}^{T})]\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Assume that Mamba model is uniformly contractive: there exists <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{A_{t}}\|_{2}\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{A_{t}}\|_{2}\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and bounded operator/Frobenius norms <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|C_{t}\|_{2}\leq c,\|\bar{B}_{t}\|_{2}\leq b,\|W_{h^{\prime}}\|_{2}\leq h,\|W_{z}\|_{F}\leq z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|C_{t}\|_{2}\leq c,\|\bar{B}_{t}\|_{2}\leq b,\|W_{h^{\prime}}\|_{2}\leq h,\|W_{z}\|_{F}\leq z</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tr}(XY)\leq\|X\|_{F}\|Y\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tr}(XY)\leq\|X\|_{F}\|Y\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and contractivity bounds,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j&lt;t}\|M_{t,j}\|_{F}^{2}\leq\frac{c^{2}b^{2}h^{2}}{1-\rho^{2}},\qquad\|M_{t,t}\|_{F}^{2}\leq c^{2}b^{2}h^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j&lt;t}\|M_{t,j}\|_{F}^{2}\leq\frac{c^{2}b^{2}h^{2}}{1-\rho^{2}},\qquad\|M_{t,t}\|_{F}^{2}\leq c^{2}b^{2}h^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}})\leq\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}z^{2}c^{2}b^{2}h^{2}\left(1+\tfrac{1}{1-\rho^{2}}\right)=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\beta_{M}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Mamba</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}})\leq\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}z^{2}c^{2}b^{2}h^{2}\left(1+\tfrac{1}{1-\rho^{2}}\right)=\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\beta_{M}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{M}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{M}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(5) Comparison and Threshold.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Collecting the bounds above, we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[St^{2}_{\mathrm{Trans}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>Trans</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[St^{2}_{\mathrm{Trans}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\|\mu_{F,\mathrm{Trans}}\|_{2}^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Trans}})=\frac{\sigma^{2}n}{4}\beta_{T}+\sigma^{2}\gamma_{T}+\alpha_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Trans</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Trans</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\|\mu_{F,\mathrm{Trans}}\|_{2}^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Trans}})=\frac{\sigma^{2}n}{4}\beta_{T}+\sigma^{2}\gamma_{T}+\alpha_{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[St^{2}_{\mathrm{Mamba}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>Mamba</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[St^{2}_{\mathrm{Mamba}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\|\mu_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}}\|_{2}^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}})\leq\frac{\sigma^{4}}{16n^{2}}\alpha_{M}+\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\beta_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Mamba</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Mamba</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\|\mu_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}}\|_{2}^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma_{F,\mathrm{Mamba}})\leq\frac{\sigma^{4}}{16n^{2}}\alpha_{M}+\frac{\sigma^{4}}{4}\beta_{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cubic form.</span> Define the cubic polynomial</p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(n)\;=\;an^{3}+bn^{2}+d," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(n)\;=\;an^{3}+bn^{2}+d,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">with</p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a:=4\sigma^{2}\beta_{T},\qquad b:=16\sigma^{2}\gamma_{T}+16\alpha_{T}-4\sigma^{4}\beta_{M},\qquad d:=-\sigma^{4}\alpha_{M}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a:=4\sigma^{2}\beta_{T},\qquad b:=16\sigma^{2}\gamma_{T}+16\alpha_{T}-4\sigma^{4}\beta_{M},\qquad d:=-\sigma^{4}\alpha_{M}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Special case <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> We aim to prove that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(1)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(1)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> in practice:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=4\sigma^{2}\beta_{T}+16\sigma^{2}\gamma_{T}+16\alpha_{T}-4\sigma^{4}\beta_{M}-\sigma^{4}\alpha_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4\sigma^{2}\beta_{T}+16\sigma^{2}\gamma_{T}+16\alpha_{T}-4\sigma^{4}\beta_{M}-\sigma^{4}\alpha_{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=16\alpha_{T}+4\sigma^{2}(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})-\sigma^{4}(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=16\alpha_{T}+4\sigma^{2}(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})-\sigma^{4}(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle Q(1)=-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(1)=-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})x^{2}+4(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})x+16\alpha_{T}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})x^{2}+4(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})x+16\alpha_{T}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\therefore\qquad\qquad\qquad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∴</mo><mspace style="width:6em;" width="6em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\therefore\qquad\qquad\qquad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})x^{2}-4(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})x-16\alpha_{T}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})x^{2}-4(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})x-16\alpha_{T}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Solve quadratic equality for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{4(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})\pm\sqrt{16(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})^{2}+64(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})\alpha_{T}}}{2(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>±</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{4(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})\pm\sqrt{16(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})^{2}+64(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})\alpha_{T}}}{2(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{4(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})\pm 4\sqrt{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})^{2}+4(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})\alpha_{T}}}{2(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{4(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})\pm 4\sqrt{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})^{2}+4(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})\alpha_{T}}}{2(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})+\sqrt{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})^{2}+4(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})\alpha_{T}}}{2\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M}/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})+\sqrt{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})^{2}+4(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})\alpha_{T}}}{2\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M}/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Note that we take the positive root with “+” because the parabola opens downward (coefficient of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> negative in original <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(1)</annotation></semantics></math>) and the soluition with “+” gives the upper bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(1)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(1)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}\leq x_{\max}:=\frac{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})+\sqrt{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})^{2}+4(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})\alpha_{T}}}{2\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M}/2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}\leq x_{\max}:=\frac{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})+\sqrt{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})^{2}+4(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})\alpha_{T}}}{2\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M}/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Given that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{T}&gt;0,\beta_{T}&gt;0,\alpha_{M}&gt;0,\beta_{M}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{T}&gt;0,\beta_{T}&gt;0,\alpha_{M}&gt;0,\beta_{M}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})+\sqrt{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})^{2}+4(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})\alpha_{T}}}{4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M}}\geq\frac{4\gamma_{T}+\sqrt{(4\gamma_{T})^{2}+0}}{4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M}}=\frac{8\gamma_{T}}{4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})+\sqrt{(\beta_{T}+4\gamma_{T})^{2}+4(4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M})\alpha_{T}}}{4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M}}\geq\frac{4\gamma_{T}+\sqrt{(4\gamma_{T})^{2}+0}}{4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M}}=\frac{8\gamma_{T}}{4\beta_{M}+\alpha_{M}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{T}\geq d&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{T}\geq d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{M},\alpha_{M}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{M},\alpha_{M}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are small, this implies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{\max}\gg 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≫</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{\max}\gg 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, for any typical choice of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}&lt;1\ll\sigma^{2}_{\max}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad Q(1)&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≪</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}&lt;1\ll\sigma^{2}_{\max}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad Q(1)&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">General case <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> As <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(1)=a+b+d&gt;0,d&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(1)=a+b+d&gt;0,d&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. We now compare <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(n)</annotation></semantics></math> vs <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(n)-Q(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(n)-Q(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=an^{3}+bn^{2}-a-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=an^{3}+bn^{2}-a-b</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a(n-1)(n^{2}+n+1)+b(n-1)(n+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a(n-1)(n^{2}+n+1)+b(n-1)(n+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(n-1)[an^{2}+(a+b)(n+1)]&gt;0\qquad\forall n&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(n-1)[an^{2}+(a+b)(n+1)]&gt;0\qquad\forall n&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\therefore\qquad\qquad Q(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∴</mo><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\therefore\qquad\qquad Q(n)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;Q(1)&gt;0\qquad\forall n&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;Q(1)&gt;0\qquad\forall n&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we conclude that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(n)&gt;0\quad\forall n\geq 1\Leftrightarrow\mathbb{E}[St^{2}_{\mathrm{Trans}}]&gt;\mathbb{E}[St^{2}_{\mathrm{Mamba}}]\quad\forall n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>Trans</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>Mamba</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(n)&gt;0\quad\forall n\geq 1\Leftrightarrow\mathbb{E}[St^{2}_{\mathrm{Trans}}]&gt;\mathbb{E}[St^{2}_{\mathrm{Mamba}}]\quad\forall n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p14.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Multi-layer Stability: From <math id="A1.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L{=}1</annotation></semantics></math> to Depth-<math id="A1.SS3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup and notation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(0)},h^{(1)},\dots,h^{(L)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(0)},h^{(1)},\dots,h^{(L)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the layer activations with
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(l+1)}\!=\!F_{l}(h^{(l)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(l+1)}\!=\!F_{l}(h^{(l)})</annotation></semantics></math> for blocks <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> (Transformer or Mamba), and write layer increments
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(l)}\!\triangleq\!h^{(l+1)}{-}h^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≜</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(l)}\!\triangleq\!h^{(l+1)}{-}h^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> and the layerwise mean <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{h}\!\triangleq\!\frac{1}{L+1}\sum_{l=0}^{L}h^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≜</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{h}\!\triangleq\!\frac{1}{L+1}\sum_{l=0}^{L}h^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the path energy <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}\!\triangleq\!\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\|\Delta^{(l)}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>path</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.0539em">≜</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.0539em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}\!\triangleq\!\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\|\Delta^{(l)}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and the depth-<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> stability</p>
<table id="A1.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}\;\triangleq\;\frac{1}{nd}\cdot\frac{1}{L+1}\sum_{l=0}^{L}\|h^{(l)}-\bar{h}\|_{F}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>St</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">≜</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}\;\triangleq\;\frac{1}{nd}\cdot\frac{1}{L+1}\sum_{l=0}^{L}\|h^{(l)}-\bar{h}\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumptioninner5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumptioninner">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumptioninner5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 5</span></span><span id="Thmassumptioninner5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Layer-wise centering and sub-Gaussianity)<span id="Thmassumptioninner5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumptioninner5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumptioninner5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumptioninner5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Each layer input is centered and standardized by normalization (e.g., LayerNorm), so rows of <math id="Thmassumptioninner5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> are zero-mean, isotropic, sub-Gaussian with bounded second/fourth moments; learned affine shifts are tracked in means and do not affect covariances after centering.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumptioninner6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumptioninner">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumptioninner6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 6</span></span><span id="Thmassumptioninner6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Weak dependence across tokens)<span id="Thmassumptioninner6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumptioninner6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumptioninner6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumptioninner6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Token rows form a weakly dependent process (e.g., <math id="Thmassumptioninner6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-mixing or <math id="Thmassumptioninner6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-weak dependence) with summable coefficients, so cross-token covariance terms are bounded by mixing coefficients times Lipschitz moduli of <math id="Thmassumptioninner6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumptioninner7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumptioninner">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumptioninner7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 7</span></span><span id="Thmassumptioninner7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Block Lipschitz/contractivity)<span id="Thmassumptioninner7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumptioninner7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumptioninner7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumptioninner7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Each block <math id="Thmassumptioninner7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is (piecewise) Lipschitz with <math id="Thmassumptioninner7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lip}(F_{l})\!\leq\!\Lambda_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lip}(F_{l})\!\leq\!\Lambda_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, and Mamba satisfies uniform contractivity for state updates with <math id="Thmassumptioninner7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{A}_{t}\|\leq\rho&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{A}_{t}\|\leq\rho&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and bounded operators <math id="Thmassumptioninner7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|C_{t}\|\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|C_{t}\|\leq c</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmassumptioninner7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{B}_{t}\|\leq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{B}_{t}\|\leq b</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmassumptioninner7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{h^{\prime}}\|\leq h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{h^{\prime}}\|\leq h</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmassumptioninner7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{z}\|_{F}\leq z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{z}\|_{F}\leq z</annotation></semantics></math>, as in your one-layer bounds.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemmainner1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemmainner">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemmainner1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemmainner1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Discrete Poincaré on a chain)<span id="Thmlemmainner1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemmainner1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemmainner1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemmainner1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the sequence <math id="Thmlemmainner1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{h^{(l)}\}_{l=0}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{h^{(l)}\}_{l=0}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l=0}^{L}\|h^{(l)}-\bar{h}\|_{F}^{2}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{4\sin^{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{2(L+1)}\right)}\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\|h^{(l+1)}-h^{(l)}\|_{F}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l=0}^{L}\|h^{(l)}-\bar{h}\|_{F}^{2}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{4\sin^{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{2(L+1)}\right)}\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\|h^{(l+1)}-h^{(l)}\|_{F}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemmainner1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemmainner1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and thus <math id="Thmlemmainner1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{4nd\sin^{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{2(L+1)}\right)}\,\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>St</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>path</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{4nd\sin^{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{2(L+1)}\right)}\,\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemmainner2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemmainner">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemmainner2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemmainner2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Propagation of one-layer surrogates)<span id="Thmlemmainner2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemmainner2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemmainner2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemmainner2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Write <math id="Thmlemmainner2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(l)}\!=\!F_{l}(h^{(l)}){-}h^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(l)}\!=\!F_{l}(h^{(l)}){-}h^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any <math id="Thmlemmainner2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\!\leq\!l\!\leq\!L{-}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\!\leq\!l\!\leq\!L{-}1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|h^{(l+1)}-h^{(l)}\|_{F}\;\leq\;\Big(\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}\Big)\,\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|h^{(l+1)}-h^{(l)}\|_{F}\;\leq\;\Big(\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}\Big)\,\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemmainner2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemmainner2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and in SSM blocks the product admits <math id="Thmlemmainner2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}\!\leq\!C\,\rho^{L-l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}\!\leq\!C\,\rho^{L-l}</annotation></semantics></math> by uniform contractivity.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark.</span> The Lipschitz constants <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Lambda_{l}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Lambda_{l}\}</annotation></semantics></math> control how single-layer surrogates propagate to later layers.
If <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> remains bounded by a modest constant, the per-layer bounds in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemmainner2" title="Lemma 2 (Propagation of one-layer surrogates). ‣ Setup and notation. ‣ A.3 Multi-layer Stability: From 𝐿=1 to Depth-𝐿 ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> give tight control on path increments. For SSMs, uniform contractivity <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{A}_{t}\|\leq\rho&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{A}_{t}\|\leq\rho&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> yields the geometric bound
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}\leq C\,\rho^{\,L-l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}\leq C\,\rho^{\,L-l}</annotation></semantics></math> used below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lipschitz continuity of the blocks, for any <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;l</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|h^{(r)}-h^{(r-1)}\|_{F}=\|F_{r-1}(h^{(r-1)})-F_{r-1}(h^{(r-2)})\|_{F}\leq\Lambda_{r-1}\|h^{(r-1)}-h^{(r-2)}\|_{F}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|h^{(r)}-h^{(r-1)}\|_{F}=\|F_{r-1}(h^{(r-1)})-F_{r-1}(h^{(r-2)})\|_{F}\leq\Lambda_{r-1}\|h^{(r-1)}-h^{(r-2)}\|_{F},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">and iterating this bound from <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=l+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=l+1</annotation></semantics></math> up to <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=L</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|h^{(l+1)}-h^{(l)}\|_{F}\leq\Big(\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}\Big)\,\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|h^{(l+1)}-h^{(l)}\|_{F}\leq\Big(\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}\Big)\,\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">The SSM contractivity statement follows by replacing <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> for SSM blocks.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumptioninner8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumptioninner">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumptioninner8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 8</span></span><span id="Thmassumptioninner8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniform one-layer gap - quantitative form)<span id="Thmassumptioninner8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumptioninner8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumptioninner8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumptioninner8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists <math id="Thmassumptioninner8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that under matched capacity/initialization and Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumptioninner5" title="Assumption 5 (Layer-wise centering and sub-Gaussianity). ‣ Setup and notation. ‣ A.3 Multi-layer Stability: From 𝐿=1 to Depth-𝐿 ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>–<a href="#Thmassumptioninner7" title="Assumption 7 (Block Lipschitz/contractivity). ‣ Setup and notation. ‣ A.3 Multi-layer Stability: From 𝐿=1 to Depth-𝐿 ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\Big[\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F}^{2}\Big]_{\mathrm{Trans}}\geq(1+\delta)\,\mathbb{E}\Big[\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F}^{2}\Big]_{\mathrm{Mamba}}\quad\text{for all }l\in\{0,\dots,L-1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mi>Trans</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mi>Mamba</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\Big[\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F}^{2}\Big]_{\mathrm{Trans}}\geq(1+\delta)\,\mathbb{E}\Big[\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F}^{2}\Big]_{\mathrm{Mamba}}\quad\text{for all }l\in\{0,\dots,L-1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheoreminner6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theoreminner">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheoreminner6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheoreminner6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Depth-<math id="Thmtheoreminner6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> stability ordering)<span id="Thmtheoreminner6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheoreminner6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheoreminner6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheoreminner6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumptioninner5" title="Assumption 5 (Layer-wise centering and sub-Gaussianity). ‣ Setup and notation. ‣ A.3 Multi-layer Stability: From 𝐿=1 to Depth-𝐿 ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>–<a href="#Thmassumptioninner8" title="Assumption 8 (Uniform one-layer gap - quantitative form). ‣ Setup and notation. ‣ A.3 Multi-layer Stability: From 𝐿=1 to Depth-𝐿 ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, the expected path energies obey</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}\right]_{\mathrm{Trans}}\;\geq\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}\right]_{\mathrm{Mamba}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>path</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>Trans</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>path</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>Mamba</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}\right]_{\mathrm{Trans}}\;\geq\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}\right]_{\mathrm{Mamba}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheoreminner6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheoreminner6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and the depth-<math id="Thmtheoreminner6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> stabilities satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}\right]_{\mathrm{Trans}}\;\geq\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}\right]_{\mathrm{Mamba}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>St</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>Trans</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>St</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>Mamba</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}\right]_{\mathrm{Trans}}\;\geq\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}\right]_{\mathrm{Mamba}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#Thmlemmainner2" title="Lemma 2 (Propagation of one-layer surrogates). ‣ Setup and notation. ‣ A.3 Multi-layer Stability: From 𝐿=1 to Depth-𝐿 ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> we have <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta^{(l)}\|_{F}^{2}\leq\kappa_{l}^{2}\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta^{(l)}\|_{F}^{2}\leq\kappa_{l}^{2}\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{l}:=\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{l}:=\prod_{k=l+1}^{L}\Lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking expectations and summing over <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}]\leq\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\kappa_{l}^{2}\,\mathbb{E}\big[\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F}^{2}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>path</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}]\leq\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\kappa_{l}^{2}\,\mathbb{E}\big[\|F_{l}(h^{(l)})\|_{F}^{2}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumptioninner8" title="Assumption 8 (Uniform one-layer gap - quantitative form). ‣ Setup and notation. ‣ A.3 Multi-layer Stability: From 𝐿=1 to Depth-𝐿 ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> (quantitative form) each term for the Transformer dominates the Mamba counterpart by factor <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}]_{\mathrm{Trans}}\geq\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}]_{\mathrm{Mamba}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>path</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>Trans</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>path</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>Mamba</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}]_{\mathrm{Trans}}\geq\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{path}}]_{\mathrm{Mamba}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
up to the (uniformly controlled) factors <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\kappa_{l}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\kappa_{l}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally apply Lemma <a href="#Thmlemmainner1" title="Lemma 1 (Discrete Poincaré on a chain). ‣ Setup and notation. ‣ A.3 Multi-layer Stability: From 𝐿=1 to Depth-𝐿 ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and normalize by <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nd(L+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nd(L+1)</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the stated ordering for <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>St</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Transformer vs. Mamba)<span id="A1.Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If each Transformer block’s one-layer bound dominates the Mamba counterpart as established in your L=1 analysis, then the depth-<math id="A1.Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> ordering <math id="A1.Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}]_{\mathrm{Trans}}\!\geq\!\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}]_{\mathrm{Mamba}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>St</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>Trans</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>St</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>Mamba</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}]_{\mathrm{Trans}}\!\geq\!\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{St}_{L}^{2}]_{\mathrm{Mamba}}</annotation></semantics></math> holds for all <math id="A1.Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\!\geq\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\!\geq\!1</annotation></semantics></math>, with constants depending on <math id="A1.Thmcorollary1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Lambda_{l}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Lambda_{l}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and SSM contractivity <math id="A1.Thmcorollary1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remarks.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(i) The discrete Poincaré constant <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(L{+}1)^{2}/\pi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L{+}1)^{2}/\pi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is tight for a chain and can be replaced with any equivalent spectral constant of the path graph; constants do not affect the ordering conclusion, only prefactors; (ii) Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumptioninner5" title="Assumption 5 (Layer-wise centering and sub-Gaussianity). ‣ Setup and notation. ‣ A.3 Multi-layer Stability: From 𝐿=1 to Depth-𝐿 ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>–<a href="#Thmassumptioninner6" title="Assumption 6 (Weak dependence across tokens). ‣ Setup and notation. ‣ A.3 Multi-layer Stability: From 𝐿=1 to Depth-𝐿 ‣ Appendix A Mathematical Derivations ‣ A Comparative Analysis of Contextual Representation Flow in State-Space and Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> replace per-layer Gaussianity/independence with practical layer-wise centering and weak dependence; (iii) Learned affine shifts from normalization affect means but not covariances after centering, and can be tracked separately in <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> terms as in your L=1 derivations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Prompting Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following setup by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2024)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al. (2024)</a></cite>, we construct key-value pairs retrieval and multi-document question answering prompting dataset.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Key-Value pairs retrieval (kv-pairs)</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We generate <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> pairs of 128-bit randomly generated UUID.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="56.54" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 56.54" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,56.54) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 1.97 L 0 54.57 C 0 55.66 0.88 56.54 1.97 56.54 L 651.18 56.54 C 652.27 56.54 653.15 55.66 653.15 54.57 L 653.15 1.97 C 653.15 0.88 652.27 0 651.18 0 L 1.97 0 C 0.88 0 0 0.88 0 1.97 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 1.97 L 1.97 54.57 L 651.18 54.57 L 651.18 1.97 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.07em;--ltx-fo-height:1.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="28.98" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.21)" width="609.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.07em;">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Example Key-Value pair<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> 
<br class="ltx_break">"7f666c61-573f-4212-a0a9-6f90d487cd4a" : "2a1d0ba0-cfe4-4df5-987a-6ee1be2c6ac0"</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> kv-pairs are composed into one single JSON object. To test at ID <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we choose one pair as gold, insert it at ID <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, and then construct as a prompt in the format:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="205.9" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 205.9" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,205.9) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 1.97 L 0 203.93 C 0 205.02 0.88 205.9 1.97 205.9 L 651.18 205.9 C 652.27 205.9 653.15 205.02 653.15 203.93 L 653.15 1.97 C 653.15 0.88 652.27 0 651.18 0 L 1.97 0 C 0.88 0 0 0.88 0 1.97 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 1.97 L 1.97 203.93 L 651.18 203.93 L 651.18 1.97 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 182.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:12.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="178.35" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="609.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.07em;">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Extract the value corresponding to the specified key in the JSON object below.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">JSON data:
<br class="ltx_break">{
"key<sup id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">1</sup>: "value<sup id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">1</sup>",
<br class="ltx_break">“key<sup id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>": "value<sup id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>",
<br class="ltx_break">…
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">"key<sup id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">k</span></sup>": "value<sup id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.5.2" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">k</span></sup>"</span>,
<br class="ltx_break">…
<br class="ltx_break">"key<sup id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">n</span></sup>": "value<sup id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.7" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">n</span></sup>",
<br class="ltx_break">} 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Key: "key<sup id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.8" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">k</span></sup>"
<br class="ltx_break">Corresponding value:</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multi-document question answering (MDQA)</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> document setting, we randomly select one question answer pair from the dataset by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2024)</a></cite>. Subsequently we retrieve the document containing this answer and mark it as gold.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="150.17" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 150.17" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,150.17) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 1.97 L 0 148.2 C 0 149.29 0.88 150.17 1.97 150.17 L 651.18 150.17 C 652.27 150.17 653.15 149.29 653.15 148.2 L 653.15 1.97 C 653.15 0.88 652.27 0 651.18 0 L 1.97 0 C 0.88 0 0 0.88 0 1.97 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 1.97 L 1.97 148.2 L 651.18 148.2 L 651.18 1.97 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 49.76)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.07em;--ltx-fo-height:6.26em;--ltx-fo-depth:2.6em;font-size:10pt;" height="122.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 86.64)" width="609.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.07em;">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Example retrieval<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Question<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: who got the first nobel prize in physics 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Answer<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Wilhelm Conrad Röntgen 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Document<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: (Title: List of Nobel laureates in Physics) The first Nobel Prize in Physics was awarded in 1901 to Wilhelm Conrad Röntgen, of Germany, who received…</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We then sample <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> distractors, relevant documents that do not contain the answer. To test at ID <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we randomly shuffle the distractors and then insert the gold document at ID <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Example prompt with gold document at ID <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is like:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="206.82" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 206.82" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,206.82) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 1.97 L 0 204.86 C 0 205.94 0.88 206.82 1.97 206.82 L 651.18 206.82 C 652.27 206.82 653.15 205.94 653.15 204.86 L 653.15 1.97 C 653.15 0.88 652.27 0 651.18 0 L 1.97 0 C 0.88 0 0 0.88 0 1.97 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 1.97 L 1.97 204.86 L 651.18 204.86 L 651.18 1.97 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 182.67)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:12.21em;font-size:10pt;" height="179.27" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="609.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.07em;">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Write a high-quality answer for the given question using only the provided search results (some of which might be irrelevant). 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Document [1](Title: Asian Americans in science and technology) Prize in physics for discovery of the subatomic… 
<br class="ltx_break">… 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Document [<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>](Title: List of Nobel laureates in Physics) The first Nobel Prize in Physics was awarded in 1901…</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">… 
<br class="ltx_break">Document [<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>] (Title: Scientist) and pursued through a unique method, was essentially in place. Ramón y Cajal won … 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question: who got the first nobel prize in physics
<br class="ltx_break">Answer:</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
